{
  "comment": "Why: the Underdark is the one theme whose dark is alive and whose light is a threat: the glowing spores that make it bearable to walk are the same spores the colonies breathe, so the party is always among things that are awake. The table is the ecology of a mushroom cavern: oozes and slimes that live in the damp (the slime tag is the default, so every faction roll is a colony), gricks and cave spiders that come out of the stems and the soil, the drow houses that farm the place (cultists: the witch, the evoker and the illusioner stand in for the dark elf priestesses and mages) with spiders as their hounds, and floating eyes that watch from the dark. The roll bonus is plus one: the road is dark but the caps glow, so the dice need less help than on the plain Abyssal road. Everything that needs the dark is a thing that lives in the shade of the caps; nothing needs the light, because the light here is the spores and everyone has it.",
  "description": "The Underdark: forests of huge mushrooms, glowing spores, drow houses and their spiders, a black lake. The mushrooms are alive and the party is walking through their dinner.",
  "rollBonus": 1,
  "budgetScale": 1.2,
  "defaultFaction": "slime",
